<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSHealthShareUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life reads your steps, distance, active calories, heart rate and sleep from Health to show them next to your workouts. It doesn't write or share your health data.</string>
	<key>NSHealthUpdateUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life doesn't write any data to Health.</string>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life uses the camera to photograph your meals and estimate their calories, to scan food barcodes, and for your profile photo and posts.</string>
	<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life uses your location only while you record a walk or a bike ride, to measure the distance. The route never leaves your phone.</string>
	<key>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life uses your location only while you record a walk or a bike ride, to measure the distance. The route never leaves your phone.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life listens to the microphone only during a guided workout with hands-free on, to understand commands like “done” or “next”.</string>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life recognizes your voice only during a guided workout with hands-free on, so you can move to the next set or exercise without touching the screen.</string>
	<key>NSMotionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life counts your daily steps with the iPhone's motion sensor.</string>
	<key>NSSupportsLiveActivities</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life saves to Photos the cards and images you choose to save and share.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Fitness Life uses your photos to estimate a meal's calories, for your profile photo and for your posts in the community.</string>
	<!-- Only standard HTTPS: exempt from export compliance documents. -->
